# Luminary — fix/481-publish-gate-off-sends-literal-string
- date: 2026-11-08
- lead: michael-feathers
- supporting: [tony-hoare, michael-nygard]
- what-the-lead-caught: the existing test stubs `gh`, so it characterises
  the script talking to a stub and never the script talking to GitHub. The
  cure is a test that pins the wire format — assert the body is valid JSON
  with reviewers as an array, not that the function was reached.
- hoare: do_off already has a real postcondition (read back, refuse to
  claim OFF unless the read says OFF). That postcondition is why this
  failed loudly for weeks instead of silently clearing nothing.
- nygard: the failure mode is correct — gate stays ON when the write fails.
  Fail-safe, not fail-open. Do not weaken that while fixing the write.
